"} "Tennis in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1"} "1896 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "2"} "1900 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "3"} "1904 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "4"} "1906  Intercalated Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "5"} "1908 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "6"} "1912 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "7"} "1920 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "8"} "1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/TEN'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Tennis at the 2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "6 – 14 August 2016"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "5"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/898"} "Centro Olímpico de Tênis, Parque Olímpico da Barra, Barra da Tijuca, Rio de Janeiro"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Tennis was contested at every Olympic Games from 1896 through 1924 as a regular medal sport. It was then discontinued, although it was on the schedule as a demonstration sport in 1968 and 1984. Tennis returned as a full medal sport in 1988, after full-time professionals were allowed to compete at the Olympics. Unlike previous editions of tennis at the Olympics, it was decided that the events in Rio would not qualify for ATP and WTA ranking points."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Up to 2008 four events were contested: men’s and women’s singles and men’s and women’s doubles, but since 2012 there has also been a mixed doubles event. The 2016 tournament was held at the Olympic Tennis Centre, at the Barra de Tijuca Olympic Park in Rio de Janeiro, which was purpose-built for the Games with a GreenSet Grand Prix Cushion surface."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All five events were single elimination contests and each event saw the players seeded to prevent players of the same ability being drawn against other in the early part of the competition. Each country was allowed six players per gender. The singles tournaments were scheduled for 64 players, the doubles for 32 pairs, and the mixed doubles for 16 pairs."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The 64 entrants in the two singles events were made up of the top 54 ranked players on both the ATP and WTA ranking lists published directly after the French Open. The International Tennis Federation assigned two quota places and six wildcard entries for each singles tournament. The ranking lists also established the first 24 doubles entrants, with eight wildcards then being awarded. A maximum of four single’s players and two doubles pairs were allowed to participate per country. For the mixed doubles only players who already played in the singles or doubles tournament were permitted to participate."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All matches were the best of three sets, except for the men’s singles final which was the best of five sets. The tie break operated in every set, including, for the first time at the Olympics, the final one. In the mixed doubles, the third set was played as a match tie-break (10 points). Heavy rain made it impossible to play on 10 August, all matches had to be rescheduled for the next day."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With the exception of the men’s singles, won by favourite " [:a {:href "/athletes/117576"} "Andy Murray"] ", all of the events saw surprise winners. " [:a {:href "/athletes/94424"} "Serena Williams"] ", the world number one, lost her third round match, and the unseeded Puerto Rican " [:a {:href "/athletes/131459"} "Mónica Puig"] " won the first ever gold medal for her country beating Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/123599"} "Angelique Kerber"] " in the final. Serbian " [:a {:href "/athletes/117575"} "Novak Đoković"] ", also the world number one, lost his first round match against Argentinian " [:a {:href "/athletes/123588"} "Juan Martín del Potro"] ", which left Murray with a great chance to defend his title."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/94424"} "Serena"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/94425"} "Venus Williams"] ", the women’s doubles favourites, also lost their first round match, and the Russian duo " [:a {:href "/athletes/120475"} "Yekaterina Makarova"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/117640"} "Yelena Vesnina"] " won the gold medal, defeating " [:a {:href "/athletes/117612"} "Timea Bacsinszky"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/2563"} "Martina Hingis"] " from Switzerland in the final. As " [:a {:href "/athletes/107360"} "Bob"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/107361"} "Mike Bryan"] " withdrew from the men’s doubles for health reasons, and Spain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/107371"} "Rafael Nadal"] " won his second Olympic gold medal when he partnered " [:a {:href "/athletes/127202"} "Marc López"] " to victory. The mixed doubles were won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/132165"} "Bethanie Mattek-Sands"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/136373"} "Jack Sock"] "."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {